---
import PageLayout from '../../layouts/PageLayout.astro';
import SupportEmail from '../../components/SupportEmail.astro';

const title = 'Privacy Policy — Keyboard Studio';
const description =
  'Privacy Policy for Keyboard Studio. Learn how typing data, phrases, settings, Full Access, and local storage are handled.';
const effectiveDate = 'July 28, 2026';
const lastUpdated = 'August 13, 2026';
---

<PageLayout title={title} description={description} canonicalPath="/privacy/">
  <div class="page-hero">
    <div class="container container--narrow">
      <h1>Keyboard Studio Privacy Policy</h1>
      <p>
        This Privacy Policy describes how the developer of Keyboard Studio handles
        information in the Keyboard Studio App and Keyboard Extension for iPhone
        and iPad.
      </p>
      <div class="meta-row">
        <span>Effective Date: {effectiveDate}</span>
        <span>Last Updated: {lastUpdated}</span>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="container container--narrow prose" style="padding-bottom: 4rem;">
    <nav class="toc" aria-labelledby="toc-heading">
      <p class="toc__title" id="toc-heading">On this page</p>
      <ol>
        <li><a href="#scope">Product scope</a></li>
        <li><a href="#collection">Developer collection practices</a></li>
        <li><a href="#local-storage">Local storage</a></li>
        <li><a href="#typed-text">Typed text</a></li>
        <li><a href="#document-context">Document context</a></li>
        <li><a href="#phrases">Quick Phrases</a></li>
        <li><a href="#dictionary">Personal Dictionary</a></li>
        <li><a href="#candidates">Local candidates and autocorrection</a></li>
        <li><a href="#emoji">Emoji search</a></li>
        <li><a href="#swipe">Swipe typing</a></li>
        <li><a href="#themes">Themes and customization</a></li>
        <li><a href="#photo-background">Photo Background</a></li>
        <li><a href="#esdb">Bundled ESDB lexicon</a></li>
        <li><a href="#full-access">Full Access</a></li>
        <li><a href="#app-group">Local App Group sharing</a></li>
        <li><a href="#feedback">Sound and haptic feedback</a></li>
        <li><a href="#network">Network access</a></li>
        <li><a href="#analytics">Analytics, tracking, and advertising</a></li>
        <li><a href="#sdks">Third-party SDKs</a></li>
        <li><a href="#accounts">Accounts and cloud services</a></li>
        <li><a href="#children">Children</a></li>
        <li><a href="#deletion">Data deletion</a></li>
        <li><a href="#changes">Changes to this policy</a></li>
        <li><a href="#contact">Contact</a></li>
      </ol>
    </nav>

    <h2 id="scope">Product scope</h2>
    <p>
      This policy applies to Keyboard Studio, including the containing App and the
      Keyboard Extension, for iPhone and iPad. It describes data practices of the
      developer of Keyboard Studio and the App itself. It does not describe every
      form of diagnostic or system data that Apple or the operating system may
      process independently of the developer.
    </p>

    <h2 id="collection">Developer collection practices</h2>
    <p>
      <strong>Keyboard Studio does not sell user data.</strong> It requires no user
      account and includes no advertising, analytics service, behavioral tracking,
      server-side keyboard prediction, or cloud typing service. The developer does
      not operate a backend service that receives typed text, document context,
      swipe paths, Emoji searches, Quick Phrases, Personal Dictionary entries, or
      keyboard settings from Keyboard Studio.
    </p>

    <h2 id="local-storage">Local storage</h2>
    <p>
      <strong>
        Quick Phrases, Personal Dictionary entries, customizations, and settings are
        stored locally.
      </strong>
      Data created or configured in Keyboard Studio remains on your device, subject
      to normal iOS storage behavior and optional local App Group sharing described
      below.
    </p>

    <h2 id="typed-text">Typed text</h2>
    <p>
      Keyboard input used for supported typing functions is processed locally while
      the keyboard operates. Keyboard Studio does not upload typed text for candidate
      generation, prediction, or other server-side keyboard processing.
    </p>

    <h2 id="document-context">Document context</h2>
    <p>
      While the keyboard is active, supported typing functions may inspect text or
      document context made available by iOS. That context is processed locally for
      the current keyboard operation; Keyboard Studio does not upload it to a
      Keyboard Studio server or save host-application text as persistent user data.
    </p>

    <h2 id="phrases">Quick Phrases</h2>
    <p>
      Quick Phrases you create are stored locally. When Full Access is enabled,
      phrases created in the containing App may be available to the Keyboard
      Extension through the local App Group container. Quick Phrases are not
      uploaded by Keyboard Studio. Phrases remain on the device until you remove
      them or delete the App, subject
      to normal iOS behavior.
    </p>

    <h2 id="dictionary">Personal Dictionary</h2>
    <p>
      Personal Dictionary entries you create are stored locally. When Full Access
      is enabled, entries created in the containing App may be available to the
      Keyboard Extension through the local App Group container. Personal Dictionary
      data is not uploaded by Keyboard Studio. Entries remain on the device until
      you remove them or delete the App, subject
      to normal iOS behavior.
    </p>

    <h2 id="candidates">Local candidates and autocorrection</h2>
    <p>
      Supported word candidates and optional autocorrection are generated on-device
      using local information and bundled lexical resources. Keyboard Studio does
      not provide cloud AI, server-side prediction, or remote personalization for
      these features.
    </p>

    <h2 id="emoji">Emoji search</h2>
    <p>
      Emoji are provided through a bundled catalog with local Unicode and
      CLDR-derived search information. Emoji search text is matched locally and is
      not sent to a Keyboard Studio server.
    </p>

    <h2 id="swipe">Swipe typing</h2>
    <p>
      Supported swipe typing is processed on-device. Keyboard Studio does not upload
      swipe paths or use a remote account or server to learn typing behavior.
    </p>

    <h2 id="themes">Themes and customization</h2>
    <p>
      Built-in theme choices, key appearance, key size, spacing and geometry, Touch
      Area, layouts, Split and adaptive layout options, animations, Glow, sound and
      haptic preferences, text and label settings, and related configuration are
      stored locally. These settings customize the keyboard; they are not remote
      advertising profiles.
    </p>

    <h2 id="photo-background">Photo Background</h2>
    <p>
      You choose a Photo Background through Apple’s system photo-selection
      interface. Keyboard Studio processes the selection locally, and an optimized
      or processed keyboard-background copy may be stored locally for keyboard use.
      Keyboard Studio does not upload the photo to a Keyboard Studio server. You can
      change, re-crop, or remove the selected background in the App.
    </p>

    <h2 id="esdb">Bundled ESDB lexicon</h2>
    <p>
      <strong>
        The built-in ESDB lexicon is bundled in the Keyboard Extension and operates
        offline.
      </strong>
      English Speller Database (ESDB), formerly SCOWL, is included for local
      lexicon features. Full license and attribution are available offline inside
      the Keyboard Studio App. Keyboard Studio does not claim ownership of ESDB.
    </p>

    <h2 id="full-access">Full Access</h2>
    <p>
      Allow Full Access is an iOS setting for third-party keyboards. Enabling it
      gives a keyboard additional system capabilities, which can include access to
      shared-container data and network capability. Full Access is optional;
      without it, basic typing, the bundled offline lexicon, gestures, layouts, and
      safe defaults remain available.
    </p>
    <p>
      <strong>
        Keyboard Studio uses Full Access where applicable for supported local
        configuration sharing between the App and Keyboard Extension and for
        supported iOS keyboard feedback behavior.
      </strong>
    </p>
    <p>
      Enabling Full Access does not cause Keyboard Studio to upload typed text,
      document context, swipe paths, Emoji searches, Personal Dictionary entries,
      Quick Phrases, photos, or settings. It does not create an account or activate
      advertising, analytics, behavioral tracking, server-side prediction, or a
      cloud typing service.
    </p>

    <h2 id="app-group">Local App Group sharing</h2>
    <p>
      When Full Access is enabled, settings, Quick Phrases, and Personal Dictionary
      data and other supported configuration may be shared between the Keyboard
      Studio App and Keyboard Studio keyboard extension through Apple’s local App
      Group container mechanism. This is local app-to-extension sharing, not cloud
      synchronization.
    </p>

    <h2 id="feedback">Sound and haptic feedback</h2>
    <p>
      Keyboard Studio uses supported iOS public system feedback facilities where
      available for keyboard sound and haptics. Availability and behavior can vary
      by device and iOS settings. Feedback does not require Keyboard Studio to
      transmit typed content.
    </p>

    <h2 id="network">Network access</h2>
    <p>
      The current product has no remote typing, prediction, Emoji-search, swipe,
      account, or cloud-sync service. Although iOS grants additional capabilities
      to a third-party keyboard when Full Access is enabled, Keyboard Studio does
      not use those capabilities to upload typed content or the local data described
      in this policy.
    </p>

    <h2 id="analytics">Analytics, tracking, and advertising</h2>
    <p>
      Keyboard Studio includes no analytics service, behavioral tracking, or
      advertising. It does not create advertising profiles from keyboard use.
    </p>

    <h2 id="sdks">Third-party SDKs</h2>
    <p>
      <strong>
        Keyboard Studio contains no analytics SDK, advertising SDK, account service,
        or cloud synchronization service.
      </strong>
    </p>

    <h2 id="accounts">Accounts and cloud services</h2>
    <p>
      Keyboard Studio does not provide an account system and does not operate a
      cloud synchronization service for keyboard data. Features described in this
      policy rely on local storage and, where enabled, local App Group sharing.
    </p>

    <h2 id="children">Children</h2>
    <p>
      Keyboard Studio is a general-audience keyboard product. The developer does not
      knowingly collect personal information from children through Keyboard Studio,
      because the App is not designed to collect personal information from users.
    </p>

    <h2 id="deletion">Local data retention and deletion</h2>
    <p>
      <strong>
        Local Keyboard Studio data may remain on the device until you remove an
        individual item, change or reset the relevant configuration, or delete the
        App, depending on the feature and subject to normal iOS behavior.
      </strong>
      Because Keyboard Studio does not maintain a developer-operated cloud copy of
      your phrases, dictionary entries, or settings, there is no separate remote
      deletion request process or cloud recovery for that data. Deleted local data
      may not be recoverable. You can disable Full Access at any time in iOS
      Settings.
    </p>

    <h2 id="changes">Changes to this policy</h2>
    <p>
      This Privacy Policy may be updated from time to time. The Last Updated date
      at the top of this page will change when updates are published on this
      website. Continued use of Keyboard Studio after an update means you should
      review the revised policy.
    </p>

    <h2 id="contact">Contact</h2>
    <p>
      For privacy questions about Keyboard Studio, contact the developer at
      <SupportEmail subject="Keyboard Studio Privacy" />.
    </p>
    <p>
      This page describes developer and App practices. It is not a certification of
      legal compliance and is not legal advice.
    </p>
  </div>
</PageLayout>
